  "id": "4",
  "content": "# Agent buttons on the Terminals page (web)\n\n## What to build\n\nThe Terminals page of graph-manager's web UI (`apps/graph-manager/src/web`) gets one button per agent \u2014 **Claude Code**, **Codex**, **OpenCode**, **Qwen Code** \u2014 as its main action, with **Plain terminal** as a secondary button. Clicking an agent button opens the existing New terminal dialog titled `New <label> terminal`; Create posts `{ workspaceId?, title?, agent }` to `POST /api/terminals`, shows a spinner and `Connecting tools\u2026` while the server prepares the agent (it may write and commit a config file), then opens the new terminal in a pane like a plain terminal does. Errors show in the dialog. A CLI that is not installed has its button disabled with the tooltip `<binary> is not installed`. Terminal rows of agent terminals show the agent's label as a tag.\n\nThe server side exists already (read it): `GET /api/agents` \u2192 `{ agents: [{ id: \"claude\"|\"codex\"|\"opencode\"|\"qwen\", label, installed: boolean, connect: \"inject\"|\"project-config\" }] }` (in `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/terminals.ts`); `POST /api/terminals` accepts `agent` and returns the `TerminalInfo` with `agent` (plus `connected` for Qwen Code); errors are `{ error }` with 400/409. The spec is `docs/prd/agent-tools.md` (section \"Web\", first bullets).\n\n## Context: files to read before implementing\n\n- `docs/prd/agent-tools.md` \u2014 \"Web\" section.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TerminalSidebar.tsx` (lines 45\u201376 props and head with the `New` button `data-testid=\"new-terminal\"`; lines 84\u2013132 the item row) \u2014 where the buttons and the tag go.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx` (line 140 `newOpen`; lines 193\u2013209 `create`; lines 405\u2013435 the sidebar wiring and the narrow top bar's `+` button; lines 531\u2013540 `<NewTerminalDialog \u2026>`; lines 631\u2013717 `NewTerminalDialog`) \u2014 the dialog and creation flow to extend.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.css` \u2014 sidebar styles (`.tsb-head`, `.tsb-new`, `.tsb-item\u2026`); add styles here.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/types.ts` (lines 37\u201350 `TerminalInfo`) \u2014 add `agent?` and `AgentInfo`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/api.ts` \u2014 `api`, `post`, `ApiError` (`err.error` is the server's message).\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx` (lines 1\u2013120: the `TerminalView`/`SpecView` mocks, the `serve()` fetch mock with `/api/terminals` POST, `calls()` helper) \u2014 the test pattern; extend `serve()` with `/api/agents`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/` \u2014 `Icon`, `Kbd`, and existing spinner styles (search `spinner` in `styles.css` / `Shell.css`, e.g. `.gate-spinner`) to reuse.\n\n## Patterns to follow\n\n**Types** (`web/types.ts`):\n```ts\nexport type AgentId = \"claude\" | \"codex\" | \"opencode\" | \"qwen\";\n/** `GET /api/agents` (src/server/routes/terminals.ts). */\nexport interface AgentInfo { id: AgentId; label: string; installed: boolean; connect: \"inject\" | \"project-config\" }\n// TerminalInfo\n/** The agent the terminal was opened with, if any. */\nagent?: AgentId;\n```\n\n**Loading the agents**: `Terminals.tsx` fetches `GET /api/agents` once on mount (`api<{ agents: AgentInfo[] }>(\"/api/agents\")`), keeping `[]` on failure; until loaded, render the four buttons from a static fallback list `[{id:\"claude\",label:\"Claude Code\"},\u2026]` disabled? \u2014 No: render nothing extra until loaded is acceptable, but prefer the static list with `installed: true` and let the fetch correct it, so the layout doesn't jump. A disabled button gets `title=\"<binary> is not installed\"`; binary = id (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `qwen`).\n\n**Sidebar props** (`TerminalSidebarProps`): add `agents: AgentInfo[]`, `onNewAgent(id: AgentId): void`, and `busyAgent?: AgentId` (the agent whose terminal is being created). Head markup:\n```tsx\n<div className=\"tsb-agents\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Open an agent\">\n  {p.agents.map((a) => (\n    <button key={a.id} type=\"button\" className=\"btn btn-primary tsb-agent\" data-testid={`agent-btn-${a.id}`}\n      disabled={!a.installed || p.busyAgent !== undefined}\n      title={a.installed ? `Open ${a.label} in a new terminal` : `${a.id} is not installed`}\n      onClick={() => p.onNewAgent(a.id)}>\n      {p.busyAgent === a.id ? <><span className=\"btn-spinner\" aria-hidden=\"true\" />Connecting tools\u2026</> : a.label}\n    </button>\n  ))}\n</div>\n<button type=\"button\" className=\"btn tsb-new\" title=\"Plain terminal (Ctrl Space, n)\" onClick={p.onNew} data-testid=\"new-terminal\">\n  <Icon name=\"plus\" size={14} /> Plain terminal\n</button>\n```\nKeep `data-testid=\"new-terminal\"` and the `Ctrl Space n` shortcut on the plain terminal (existing tests click it). Row tag: inside `.tsb-item-text`, after the title, `{t.agent && <span className=\"tsb-agent-tag\" data-testid={`agent-tag-${t.id}`}>{label}</span>}` with the label from `p.agents` (fallback to the id).\n\n**Dialog**: `NewTerminalDialog` gains `agent?: AgentInfo`. Title and `aria-label` become `New ${agent.label} terminal` when set. `onCreate` body gets `agent: agent.id`. While busy, the Create button is disabled and reads `Connecting tools\u2026` with the spinner (plain terminals keep `Create`). An error from the POST is shown inside the dialog (`<p className=\"field-error\" role=\"alert\" data-testid=\"new-terminal-error\">`) and the dialog stays open; today `create` in Terminals.tsx sets a page-level `error` \u2014 for agent terminals pass the error back to the dialog (e.g. make `create` return `{ info } | { error }` or throw, and let the dialog catch it). For `project-config` agents add a hint under the workspace field: `Commits .qwen/settings.json once if graph-manager's tools are not connected yet.` (use `agent.connect === \"project-config\"`; the file name may be hard-coded for qwen). Qwen Code needs a workspace: when `agent.connect === \"project-config\"` remove the \"Workspaces root\" option and preselect the default/first workspace.\n\n**State in `Terminals.tsx`**: replace `newOpen: boolean` usage by also tracking `newAgent: AgentInfo | undefined` (set on `onNewAgent`, cleared on cancel/success); `busyAgent` is the agent while its POST runs. The narrow top bar keeps its `+` (plain terminal). After success, behave exactly like the plain flow (open the pane, `overview.refresh()`).\n\n## Step-by-step tasks\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/types.ts`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `AgentId`, `AgentInfo`, `TerminalInfo.agent`.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TerminalSidebar.tsx`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: the buttons, the plain-terminal button, the agent tag.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: fetch agents, `onNewAgent`, dialog changes, busy/error handling.\n- **GOTCHA**: the page uses keyboard bindings that are disabled while a modal is open (`modal = newOpen || confirm !== null`, line ~327); keep the dialog open state in that expression.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.css`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `.tsb-agents` (wrap, small gap, full width in the sidebar head), `.tsb-agent`, `.tsb-agent-tag` (small mono pill using existing tokens, look at `.run-chip`), `.btn-spinner` (reuse an existing spinner class if there is one; otherwise a 12px border spinner with `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` disabling the animation).\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: extend `serve()` to answer `GET /api/agents` with the four agents (`codex` `installed: false`) and to accept `agent` in the POST body (return a terminal with `agent`). Tests:\n  - the four `agent-btn-*` buttons and `new-terminal` render; `agent-btn-codex` is disabled with title `codex is not installed`.\n  - click `agent-btn-claude` \u2192 dialog `New Claude Code terminal`; Create \u2192 one POST `/api/terminals` whose JSON body has `agent: \"claude\"`; while the POST is pending (make the mock await a deferred promise) the button text is `Connecting tools\u2026`; after it resolves the dialog closes and the new terminal's pane opens (`terminal-view-<id>`).\n  - a 409 `{ error: \"cannot commit .qwen/settings.json: it has uncommitted changes\" }` for qwen \u2192 the dialog stays open and shows that text in `new-terminal-error`.\n  - a terminal with `agent: \"claude\"` shows `agent-tag-<id>` with `Claude Code`.\n  - the existing plain-terminal tests still pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The Terminals sidebar shows Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Qwen Code buttons and a secondary **Plain terminal** button (`Ctrl Space n` still opens the plain dialog).\n- [ ] An agent button opens `New <label> terminal`; Create posts `agent`; while waiting it shows `Connecting tools\u2026`; success opens the terminal in a pane; an error shows in the dialog.\n- [ ] Not-installed agents are disabled with `<binary> is not installed`.\n- [ ] Agent terminals show their agent's label as a tag in the list.\n- [ ] Tests pass: `npm test -w graph-manager -- src/web`.\n- [ ] Look at the page yourself (TESTING.md \"graph-manager\": build, start the server with temp dirs, log in, open Terminals) at desktop and ~390 px width; both themes stay legible.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run build -w graph-execution && npm run build -w graph-manager\nnpm run typecheck && npm run lint\nnpm test -w graph-manager -- src/web\n```\n",
  "dependencies": [
    "3"
  ]
